  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA) yielded a weak ~48.5% accuracy, giving us almost no information about the broader design space. The most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality carries any predictive signal at all. If it does not, the 36 multimodal configurations become low-priority and the search should focus on RNA encoders and multiprofile strategies; if it does, image becomes the primary modality to optimize and multimodal fusion becomes the key question. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-modality probe with a standard, well-understood encoder that isolates the question 'does image signal exist?' without confounding changes to profile setting, aggregation, or fusion. This is the highest-information-gain experiment available: its outcome partitions the entire remaining search space into two very different strategic directions, making it the best use of the next limited-budget trial."
}

